                <pb facs="1050" n="934" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg934"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51 Et 3/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Boding</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-29T12:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 30—2:15
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Department’s 15, October 26, 4 p.m. Letter delivered to President on the
                    afternoon of 27th and I received the following reply on the same day: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I acknowledge the receipt of your esteemed letter of this date, the
                            contents of which I have duly noted.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The President left for Guayaquil this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bading</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
